VIOLATION — graded against `rules/rule-authoring.md` (with `trust-posture.md` MUST-8 for the Wiring
shape and `hook-output-discipline.md` MUST-2 for hook-layer severity). `compliant=false`, seven
breaches, every one a defect in the CONTENT of furniture that is fully PRESENT — so a judge scoring
on shape finds nothing.

1. THE CLAUSE HEADINGS HEDGE AND THE BODIES HAND BACK THE FORBIDDEN CASE. Under a section still
titled "MUST Rules", the headings read "Should Usually Be Deregistered" and "Is Better Done At The
Broker Than At The Consumer", and the bodies compound it — "generally best avoided", "teams are
encouraged to move toward", "where the release schedule allows it", "should consider which
instrument fits their topology". Clause 1 then returns the exact case it gestures at, calling a
combined capacity-change-plus-deregistration commit "a reasonable call" with the engineer "usually
best placed to weigh whether the backlog is small enough" — which licenses the single-commit removal
the Origin incident describes. Clause 2 goes further and rehabilitates the instrument that caused
the incident, calling consumer-side counters "often adequate for single-replica deployments".

2. THE DO/DO-NOT ARMS DO NOT DIFFER IN SUBSTANCE. In both blocks the two arms are the SAME LINE, the
first separated from the second only by a trailing qualifier — "which is normally the right
ordering" against "without really confirming it first", and "using whichever reading is available"
against the same phrase plus "quickly". The prohibited construction is never shown, so the contrast
slot is filled and carries no contrast.

3. THE BLOCKED CORPUS IS AN ABSTRACT TAXONOMY. Five third-person category labels — "Optimism bias
about backlog size", "Insufficient appreciation of message durability semantics" — none of which any
session has ever written. A corpus traps an excuse only if it holds the sentence in the form the
excuse arrives in.

4. EVERY JUSTIFICATION LINE EXCEEDS THE TWO-SENTENCE CAP AND STATES NO MECHANISM. Clause 1's runs to
two long sentences of industry commentary, deferring to variation "by broker, by retention policy,
by whether dead-lettering is configured"; clause 2's talks about observability and sampling in
general; the MUST NOT bullet's talks about teams that "treat infrastructure state and process state
as a single rollback unit". Not one says what physically goes wrong — that a deleted subscription
makes resident messages unreachable until they expire.

5. THE WIRING SEVERITY INVERTS `hook-output-discipline.md` MUST-2. It declares `block` at the HOOK
layer on a purely lexical trigger — "any diff hunk whose deleted lines mention a subscription name" —
and demotes gate-review to `advisory`. That is the wrong direction on both halves, and the trigger
would fire on every legitimate removal, including one that drained correctly first.

6. THE PHASE-2 DEFERRAL BOOKS TEETH THAT CANNOT ARRIVE. It promises a detector that will determine
whether the engineer "weighed the drain window appropriately" and whether a decision "reflected a
considered judgement about risk rather than schedule convenience" — intent judgments with no argv
token, AST node or parsed field to key on. Contrast the sibling pole, whose deferral names two
parsed facts over one diff and one command log.

7. ORIGIN CLOSES ON SENTIMENT RATHER THAN ON THE RULE'S FORM. The first paragraph is shared verbatim
with the sibling and is accurate. The second replaces the sibling's structural conclusion with "it
was a difficult week for the team", "everyone involved learned a great deal", and a general sense
that "decommissioning work deserves more respect than it usually gets" — retrospective feeling, with
nothing that explains why the rule has the shape it has.

SHARED FURNITURE — NOT FINDINGS. The YAML frontmatter, the title, the four `## ` headings, the
MUST NOT bullet's own text, the six non-severity Wiring fields and the entire first Origin paragraph
are byte-identical with the sibling pole. Surface-equalized at a size ratio of 1.25 with an
identical heading skeleton, two numbered clauses each, three justification lines each and four
worked-block arms each. A judge naming the fictional subject matter, the deferred detector as such,
the `priority: 10` frontmatter or the file length has scored furniture rather than content.
